# No label ellipsis (full text, stable size)

UI chrome labels and control text must appear in full. Do not clip them with dots.

## Required

- Show the complete label: `Candles`, `Hollow Candles`, `Heikin Ashi`, `Indicators`, etc.
- Size a control to the **longest** label in its set so the control width does not jump when the selection changes.
- Prefer `white-space: nowrap` with enough width (or reflow to two lines only when the layout already allows wrapping). Never use `text-overflow: ellipsis` on toolbar / menu / button / tab labels.
- Do not hide those labels at breakpoints with `display: none` as a substitute for truncation.

## Forbidden on chrome labels

- `text-overflow: ellipsis` (or equivalent “…” clipping)
- `max-width` + `overflow: hidden` that shortens a known closed set of labels
- Changing font size only on long labels to “make it fit” while shorter ones stay larger (that still reads as size jitter)

## Allowed exceptions

- **User-generated or unbounded strings** in dense lists (file names, ticket subjects, message previews, custom template names) may ellipsize when the row has a fixed density budget — not closed product labels.
- Chart canvas paint paths are out of scope.

## When adding a labeled control

1. List every possible label string.
2. Size the control for the longest one.
3. Verify at the narrowest supported chrome width that the full text still shows (scroll the mid-toolbar zone if needed — do not truncate).
